WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
In eighteen sixty-nine,

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.850
Dmitri Mendeleev sorted all the
elements he knew into a table.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.790
But he left gaps.

4
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.290
Empty boxes.

5
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.530
Then he did something bold.

6
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.550
He described the elements
that should fill those gaps,

7
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.770
before anyone had found them.

8
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.050
Years later, gallium and
germanium were found.

9
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.530
They matched his descriptions closely.

10
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.830
So how could he describe an
element nobody had found?

11
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.330
Was it a lucky guess?

12
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.830
In this mission, you'll
learn to read the table:

13
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.210
groups and periods, metals and
non-metals, and their oxides.

14
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.070
Your mission: explain how
Mendeleev described elements nobody

15
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.500
had found.
